  "notes": "Aladin Lite embedded full-screen: the astronomical image (Orion B, NGC 2024/2023 region, Alnitak bright star) is the whole page. Controls are small light-grey (#ececec) squares with 2px dark (#212121) borders and 3px radii, black filled icons, floating directly over the image with no panels. Coordinates shown in magenta (#ff54ff) monospace; magenta crosshair reticle marks view centre. Overlays colour-coded per catalog: red circles SIMBAD, teal diamonds YSO candidates, orange squares Gaia, yellow filled dots notes, lime/purple/orange polygons JWST/CFHT/KMOS/MUSE footprints, shaded orange MOC coverage. Live: layers button opens a 'Stack' panel listing overlays and surveys with eye/settings/delete buttons; clicking a source opens a bottom table of its catalog attributes."
